1
00:00:02,850 --> 00:00:06,897
SISSO doesn't hand you an answer. It hands
you a pile of candidates.

2
00:00:07,277 --> 00:00:12,082
Metrics to line up by hand. And the best
training fit may not be the best model.

3
00:00:12,462 --> 00:00:17,141
SISSO-Analyzer puts every candidate in one
table: sortable metrics,

4
00:00:17,141 --> 00:00:21,041
a Pareto front, and the full formula
behind every point.

5
00:00:21,421 --> 00:00:24,981
Open one: predictions, residuals,
comparisons.

6
00:00:24,981 --> 00:00:28,308
Copy it as LaTeX, straight into your
paper.

7
00:00:28,688 --> 00:00:31,240
SISSO-Sage gives your agent the evidence:

8
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:35,160
shortlist models that balance prediction
with physical meaning,

9
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,463
and trace each feature to its source.

10
00:00:37,843 --> 00:00:39,574
One engine. Two readers.

11
00:00:39,954 --> 00:00:43,051
From a pile of candidates, to the ones you
can defend.

